From 5d443b3f962fc84e6dc312d1a406350f2053e516 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guillermo Vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:24:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop: Don't advertise AFBC on the RK3399 primary
 plane

The RK3399 VOP AFBC decoder only supports frames up to 2560x1600
(datasheet, "1.2.10 Video IN/OUT": "Support AFBC function co-operation
with GPU: support 2560x1600 UI"). Panfrost picks AFBC for the scanout
buffer whenever the primary plane advertises it, so 4K outputs show
corruption on the right side of the screen.

The plane's modifier list is fixed at init and can't depend on the
mode. Rejecting wider AFBC framebuffers instead, as proposed in [1],
breaks userspace that doesn't fall back to linear: Weston fails with
"failed to create kms fb: Invalid argument" and the output stays black.

Stop advertising AFBC on the primary plane so userspace always
allocates a linear scanout buffer. The GPU still uses AFBC internally
and for buffers shared between clients and the compositor.

Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/7968
[1]: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20250604090054.7070-1-mail@etehtsea.me/

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [disable feature]
Signed-off-by: Guillermo Vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
index f7d0edd..6d9687e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop_reg.c
@@ -962,12 +962,14 @@ static const struct vop_win_phy rk3399_win01_data = {
 };
 
 /*
- * rk3399 vop big windows register layout is same as rk3288, but we
- * have a separate rk3399 win data array here so that we can advertise
- * AFBC on the primary plane.
+ * rk3399 vop big windows register layout is same as rk3288. AFBC is not
+ * advertised on the primary plane: the AFBC decoder only supports up to
+ * 2560x1600, the modifier list can't depend on the mode, and userspace
+ * that composites to an AFBC primary plane doesn't fall back to linear
+ * when a wider AFBC framebuffer is rejected.
  */
 static const struct vop_win_data rk3399_vop_win_data[] = {
-	{ .base = 0x00, .phy = &rk3399_win01_data,
+	{ .base = 0x00, .phy = &rk3368_win01_data,
 	  .type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY },
 	{ .base = 0x40, .phy = &rk3368_win01_data,
 	  .type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY },
